            {
              "text": "Because \"Newcastle\" frequently refers to either **Newcastle upon Tyne (UK)** or **Newcastle, New South Wales (Australia)**, the leading Microsoft Power BI and Microsoft Fabric consultancies specializing in data warehousing and operational reporting are broken down by region below.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Newcastle upon Tyne, UK (North East England)\n\nIf you are based in the UK, Newcastle has developed a strong data and tech hub around areas like Newcastle Helix and Hoults Yard. The top local consultancies include:\n\n*   **Seriös Group** *(Hoults Yard, Newcastle upon Tyne)*  \n    * **Focus:** Enterprise data platform engineering, data warehousing, and advanced analytics.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** One of the most prominent data-first consultancies based directly in Newcastle. They specialize in guiding companies through migrations to **Microsoft Fabric**, building Lakehouse/Warehouse architectures, setting up automated ETL via Data Factory, and designing high-performing Power BI semantic layers.\n*   **Marra** *(Newcastle Helix, Newcastle upon Tyne)*  \n    * **Focus:** Microsoft Power Platform and operational business intelligence.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** Headquartered at the Newcastle Helix tech cluster, Marra focuses on turning fragmented operational data (ERP, CRM, Dynamics 365) into interactive dashboards. They emphasize operational reporting automation and business process optimization.\n*   **Geordie Consulting** *(Newcastle upon Tyne)*  \n    * **Focus:** Microsoft Power BI, Power Platform, and business analytics.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** A boutique, regionally dedicated Microsoft Partner that focuses on data modeling, DAX performance tuning, report development, and user upskilling for mid-market businesses.\n*   **EchoBI** *(North East / Newcastle & Northumberland)*  \n    * **Focus:** Practical operational reporting and data integration.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** EchoBI specializes in bridging the gap between raw back-office systems (finance, inventory, ERPs) and executive dashboards. They build the underlying data pipelines and warehousing models to ensure operational reporting is stable and trusted.\n*   **DHS IT Solutions** *(Newcastle upon Tyne)*  \n    * **Focus:** Cloud infrastructure, data modernization, and enterprise architecture.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** Architects modern data estates leveraging Microsoft Fabric, Azure Synapse, and Power BI to unify siloed data environments.\n*   **National UK Microsoft Solutions Partners (with strong North East delivery):**  \n    * **Advancing Analytics** & **BCN Group:** If you require enterprise-tier migration support (e.g., migrating legacy SQL Server data warehouses to Fabric OneLake / Direct Lake mode), these UK-wide Microsoft Solutions Partners have dedicated data and AI practices operating across the North East.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Newcastle, New South Wales (Hunter Region, Australia)\n\nIf you are located in the Hunter/Newcastle region of Australia, top consultants with local presence or direct regional delivery include:\n\n*   **SSW (Newcastle Office)**  \n    * **Focus:** Enterprise software architecture, Azure data warehousing, and Microsoft ecosystem solutions.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** SSW has an established physical presence in Newcastle. As an accredited Microsoft Solutions Partner, they design enterprise-grade data warehouses, Medallion architecture (Bronze/Silver/Gold in OneLake), and end-to-end Power BI operational dashboards.\n*   **Evocate** *(Newcastle / Hunter Valley)*  \n    * **Focus:** Modern workplace and Microsoft Cloud data solutions.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** They provide consulting services focused on Microsoft Fabric readiness, Power BI governance, and cross-platform operational analytics tailored to regional mid-market companies.\n*   **Breadcrumb Digital & Lanter Technologies** *(Servicing NSW / Newcastle Region)*  \n    * **Focus:** Dedicated Microsoft Fabric implementation, data governance, and analytics strategy.\n    * **Fabric & Power BI Capabilities:** Certified Fabric partners who specialize in architecting OneLake data structures, Direct Lake modeling, and multi-source operational reporting for healthcare, logistics, and infrastructure clients across New South Wales.\n\n---\n\n### Key Capabilities to Look For\n\nWhen evaluating these consultants for **operational reporting** and **data warehousing**, confirm they provide:\n1. **Microsoft Fabric Capacity & Cost Governance:** Expertise in Fabric sizing (F-SKUs) to avoid runaway compute bills while running scheduled warehouse pipelines.\n2. **Direct Lake & Semantic Modeling:** Experience implementing Direct Lake mode over Delta tables to deliver real-time operational reporting without traditional Power BI import refresh delays.\n3. **Medallion Architecture Design:** Building Bronze (raw), Silver (cleansed), and Gold (modeled star-schema) layers within Fabric Lakehouses/Warehouses to ensure data consistency across departments.\n4. **Data Governance & Row-Level Security (RLS):** Aligning access control across Microsoft Purview and Power BI workspaces so staff only see operations-relevant data.",
